  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.close": "Close guide",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.overview.title": "1. Basic flow",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.overview.body": "Choose a battle format and session rules, select the Pokémon that will enter, and build a win streak. Single battles use 3 Pokémon and Double battles use 4.",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.registration.title": "2. Registration rules",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.registration.body": "You need a party of 6 when you first confirm a team. All six must be different species and held items cannot be duplicated. Bag items are disabled in battle. Pokémon above level 50 are set to level 50 on their battle copy.",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.setup.title": "3. Before the first battle",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.setup.body": "Choose Single or Double, then choose one mechanic: Mega Evolution, Dynamax, or Terastallization. Each side may use that mechanic once per battle. After the first battle starts, it cannot be changed until the run ends.",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.legendary.title": "4. Legendary Class",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.legendary.body": "Legendary Class includes Legendary, Mythical, Ultra Beast, and Paradox Pokémon. When disallowed, neither side can select them. Allowing them only adds them to each side's eligible pool; it does not force either side to use one. This option also locks after the first battle.",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.registered_team.title": "5. Your registered six stay fixed",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.registered_team.body": "The 6 Pokémon registered at the first confirmation are stored separately until the run ends. Changing your adventure party does not change the Battle Tower team. Change Team only reselects the 3 or 4 entrants from those registered six. The registered team is discarded when the session ends through a forfeit or disconnect.",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.progression.title": "6. Streaks and rewards",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.progression.body": "A win updates the current and best streak and awards the BP shown on the screen. Every fifth win is a boss battle with bonus BP. Higher streaks advance through Introductory, Practical, Advanced, and Pro stages. A loss resets the current streak to 0 while preserving the best streak.",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.controls.title": "7. Controls",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.controls.body": "The order in which you click Pokémon cards becomes their battle order. Confirm Team validates the registration and selection; Start enters the next battle. Change Team does not replace the registered six. The X in the top right only closes the screen, and reopening it returns to the active session.",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.troubleshooting.title": "8. If the battle will not start",
  "screen.more_cobblemon_contents.tower.guide.troubleshooting.body": "If Confirm Team is disabled, check the required selection count, mechanic choice, party size of 6, and duplicate species or held items. If the adventure party changed before the first confirmation, reopen the screen. Mechanic and Legendary Class controls that turn gray after the first battle can be changed again only after the current run ends.",
